  "title": "LS2 fix round 2: drop the module-level test wrappers added in 21e3bd9",
  "spec": "Fix round of T-1596 (chain T-1593). Commit 21e3bd9 added module-level functions test_write_keeps_sections_after_handover and test_write_twice_stays_idempotent_with_tail at tests/test_handover.py:17-22 that call Handover(...).debug(). The gate (orchestrator/acceptance.py missing_tests) treats any column-0 `def <name>(` as a test unittest does not collect, so these wrappers are what now fails the gate. Remove exactly those module-level wrappers (run `git revert --no-edit 21e3bd9` or delete lines 17-22); keep the methods inside class Handover (lines ~206 and ~222) unchanged. Do not add module-level test functions. Run the tests in tests/test_handover.py with unittest and commit.",
